IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cla-nouns`
IMPORT `cla-p08-wrongful-death`

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 1 -- sections 15 to 19: contribution between persons liable for the same damage.
--
-- This module imports cla-p08-wrongful-death.l4 only for section 19(3)(a), where "dependants" "has the same meaning as in section 20":
-- that answer is section 20(8)'s, not a second copy of it.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer".

§ `Section 15 -- entitlement to contribution`

-- src:1124 | 15.—(1) Subject to subsections (2) to (5), any person liable in
-- src:1125 | respect of any damage suffered by another person may recover
-- src:1126 | contribution from any other person liable in respect of the same
-- src:1127 | damage (whether jointly with him or otherwise).
@ref s 15(1) (src:1124-1127)
GIVEN `the person is liable in respect of damage suffered by another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is liable in respect of the same damage whether jointly with him or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(1) the person may recover contribution from the other person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is liable in respect of damage suffered by another person` AND `the other person is liable in respect of the same damage whether jointly with him or otherwise` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person liable in respect of any damage suffered by another person may recover contribution from any other person liable in respect of the same damage" -- subject to subsections (2) to (5), which have their own functions

-- src:1129 | (2) A person shall be entitled to recover contribution by virtue of
-- src:1130 | subsection (1) notwithstanding that he has ceased to be liable in
-- src:1131 | respect of the damage in question since the time when the damage
-- src:1132 | occurred, provided that he was so liable immediately before he made
-- src:1133 | or was ordered or agreed to make the payment in respect of which the
-- src:1134 | contribution is sought.
@ref s 15(2) (src:1129-1134)
GIVEN `the person has ceased to be liable in respect of the damage since the time when the damage occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he was so liable immediately before he made or was ordered or agreed to make the payment in respect of which the contribution is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(2) the person is entitled to recover contribution although he has ceased to be liable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person has ceased to be liable in respect of the damage since the time when the damage occurred` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "notwithstanding that he has ceased to be liable in respect of the damage in question since the time when the damage occurred"
        IF `he was so liable immediately before he made or was ordered or agreed to make the payment in respect of which the contribution is sought` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that he was so liable immediately before he made or was ordered or agreed to make the payment in respect of which the contribution is sought"

-- src:1136 | (3) A person shall be liable to make contribution by virtue of
-- src:1137 | subsection (1) notwithstanding that he has ceased to be liable in
-- src:1138 | respect of the damage in question since the time when the damage
-- src:1139 | occurred, unless he ceased to be liable by virtue of the expiry of a
-- src:1140 | period of limitation or prescriptions which extinguished the right on
-- src:1141 | which the claim against him in respect of the damage was based.
@ref s 15(3) (src:1136-1141)
GIVEN `the person has ceased to be liable in respect of the damage since the time when the damage occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he ceased to be liable by virtue of the expiry of a period of limitation or prescription which extinguished the right on which the claim against him in respect of the damage was based` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(3) the person is liable to make contribution although he has ceased to be liable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person has ceased to be liable in respect of the damage since the time when the damage occurred` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "notwithstanding that he has ceased to be liable in respect of the damage in question since the time when the damage occurred"
        IF `he ceased to be liable by virtue of the expiry of a period of limitation or prescription which extinguished the right on which the claim against him in respect of the damage was based` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he ceased to be liable by virtue of the expiry of a period of limitation or prescription which extinguished the right on which the claim against him in respect of the damage was based" -- an exception to a liability: the requirement does not apply (not question QA, which is about a lifted bar)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1143 | (4) A person who has made or agreed to make any payment in bona
-- src:1144 | fide settlement or compromise of any claim made against him in
-- src:1145 | respect of any damage (including a payment into court which has
-- src:1146 | been accepted) shall be entitled to recover contribution in accordance
-- src:1151 | with this section without regard to whether or not he himself is or ever
-- src:1152 | was liable in respect of the damage, provided, however, that he would
-- src:1153 | have been liable assuming that the factual basis of the claim against
-- src:1154 | him could be established.
@ref s 15(4) (src:1143-1154)
GIVEN `the person has made or agreed to make a payment in bona fide settlement or compromise of a claim made against him in respect of damage including a payment into court which has been accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he would have been liable assuming that the factual basis of the claim against him could be established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(4) the person is entitled to recover contribution in accordance with section 15 whether or not he was liable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person has made or agreed to make a payment in bona fide settlement or compromise of a claim made against him in respect of damage including a payment into court which has been accepted` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who has made or agreed to make any payment in bona fide settlement or compromise of any claim made against him in respect of any damage (including a payment into court which has been accepted)"
        IF `he would have been liable assuming that the factual basis of the claim against him could be established` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided, however, that he would have been liable assuming that the factual basis of the claim against him could be established"

-- src:1156 | (5) A judgment given in any action brought in Singapore by or on
-- src:1157 | behalf of the person who suffered the damage in question against any
-- src:1158 | person from whom contribution is sought under this section shall be
-- src:1159 | conclusive in the proceedings for contribution in favour of the person
-- src:1160 | from whom the contribution is sought, provided that the judgment in
-- src:1161 | his favour rested on a determination of the merits of the claim against
-- src:1162 | him in respect of the damage.
@ref s 15(5) (src:1156-1162)
GIVEN `the judgment was given in an action brought in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage against the person from whom contribution is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment in his favour rested on a determination of the merits of the claim against him in respect of the damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(5) the judgment is conclusive in the proceedings for contribution in favour of the person from whom contribution is sought` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judgment was given in an action brought in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage against the person from whom contribution is sought` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judgment given in any action brought in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage in question against any person from whom contribution is sought under this section"
        IF `the judgment in his favour rested on a determination of the merits of the claim against him in respect of the damage` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that the judgment in his favour rested on a determination of the merits of the claim against him in respect of the damage"

-- src:1164 | (6) References in this section to a person’s liability in respect of any
-- src:1165 | damage are references to any such liability which has been or could
-- src:1166 | be established in an action brought against him in Singapore by or on
@ref s 15(6) (src:1164-1166)
GIVEN `the liability has been or could be established in an action brought against him in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(6) the liability is a liability in respect of damage for the purposes of section 15` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the liability has been or could be established in an action brought against him in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this section to a person's liability in respect of any damage are references to any such liability which has been or could be established in an action brought against him in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage"

-- src:1167 | behalf of the person who suffered the damage; but it is immaterial
-- src:1168 | whether any issues arising in any such action was or would be
-- src:1169 | determined (in accordance with the rules of private international law)
-- src:1170 | by reference to the law of a country outside Singapore.
@ref s 15(6) the foreign law (src:1167-1170)
GIVEN `an issue in the action was or would be determined in accordance with the rules of private international law by reference to the law of a country outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(6) it matters that an issue was or would be determined by reference to the law of a country outside Singapore` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an issue in the action was or would be determined in accordance with the rules of private international law by reference to the law of a country outside Singapore` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is immaterial whether any issues arising in any such action was or would be determined (in accordance with the rules of private international law) by reference to the law of a country outside Singapore"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reference to the law of a country outside Singapore"

§ `Section 16 -- assessment of contribution`

-- src:1174 | 16.—(1) Subject to subsection (3), in any proceedings for
-- src:1175 | contribution under section 15, the amount of the contribution
-- src:1176 | recoverable from any person shall be such as may be found by the
-- src:1177 | court to be just and equitable having regard to the extent of that
-- src:1178 | person’s responsibility for the damage in question.
@ref s 16(1) (src:1174-1178)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings for contribution under section 15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is one the court finds just and equitable having regard to the extent of the person's responsibility for the damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(1) the amount of the contribution is the amount the court finds just and equitable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are proceedings for contribution under section 15` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any proceedings for contribution under section 15"
        IF `the amount is one the court finds just and equitable having regard to the extent of the person's responsibility for the damage` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "shall be" (fork QB); the subsection fixes the standard and no figure

-- src:1180 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), the court shall have power in any such
-- src:1181 | proceedings to exempt any person from liability to make
-- src:1182 | contribution, or to direct that the contribution to be recovered from
-- src:1183 | any person shall amount to a complete indemnity.
@ref s 16(2) (src:1180-1183)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings for contribution under section 15` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(2) the court has power to exempt the person from liability to make contribution or to direct a complete indemnity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings are proceedings for contribution under section 15` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any such proceedings"

-- src:1185 | (3) Where the amount of the damages which have or might have
-- src:1186 | been awarded in respect of the damage in question in any action
-- src:1187 | brought in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered it
-- src:1188 | against the person from whom the contribution is sought was or
-- src:1189 | would have been subject to —
-- src:1191 | (a) any limit imposed by or under any written law or by any
-- src:1192 | agreement made before the damage occurred;
-- src:1197 | (b) any reduction by virtue of section 3 of the Contributory
-- src:1198 | Negligence and Personal Injuries Act 1953; or
-- src:1200 | (c) any corresponding limit or reduction under the law of a
-- src:1201 | country outside Singapore,
-- src:1203 | the person from whom the contribution is sought shall not, by virtue
-- src:1204 | of any contribution awarded under section 15, be required to pay in
-- src:1205 | respect of the damage a greater amount than the amount of those
-- src:1206 | damages as so limited or reduced.
@ref s 16(3) the cap (src:1185-1206)
GIVEN `the damages would have been awarded in an action brought in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage against the person from whom the contribution is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were or would have been subject to a limit imposed by or under any written law or by an agreement made before the damage occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were or would have been subject to a reduction by virtue of section 3 of the Contributory Negligence and Personal Injuries Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were or would have been subject to a corresponding limit or reduction under the law of a country outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contribution awarded under section 15` IS A NUMBER
      `the damages as so limited or reduced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 16(3) the most the person is required to pay in respect of the damage by virtue of the contribution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 16(3) the cap applies` `the damages would have been awarded in an action brought in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage against the person from whom the contribution is sought` `they were or would have been subject to a limit imposed by or under any written law or by an agreement made before the damage occurred` `they were or would have been subject to a reduction by virtue of section 3 of the Contributory Negligence and Personal Injuries Act 1953` `they were or would have been subject to a corresponding limit or reduction under the law of a country outside Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the amount of the damages ... was or would have been subject to — (a) any limit ...; (b) any reduction ...; or (c) any corresponding limit or reduction"
        OTHERWISE JUST (min `the contribution awarded under section 15` `the damages as so limited or reduced`)

-- src:1185 | (3) Where the amount of the damages which have or might have
-- src:1186 | been awarded in respect of the damage in question in any action
-- src:1187 | brought in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered it
-- src:1188 | against the person from whom the contribution is sought was or
-- src:1189 | would have been subject to —
-- src:1191 | (a) any limit imposed by or under any written law or by any
-- src:1192 | agreement made before the damage occurred;
-- src:1197 | (b) any reduction by virtue of section 3 of the Contributory
-- src:1198 | Negligence and Personal Injuries Act 1953; or
-- src:1200 | (c) any corresponding limit or reduction under the law of a
-- src:1201 | country outside Singapore,
-- src:1203 | the person from whom the contribution is sought shall not, by virtue
-- src:1204 | of any contribution awarded under section 15, be required to pay in
-- src:1205 | respect of the damage a greater amount than the amount of those
-- src:1206 | damages as so limited or reduced.
@ref s 16(3) the cap applies (src:1185-1206)
GIVEN `the damages would have been awarded in an action brought in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage against the person from whom the contribution is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were or would have been subject to a limit imposed by or under any written law or by an agreement made before the damage occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were or would have been subject to a reduction by virtue of section 3 of the Contributory Negligence and Personal Injuries Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were or would have been subject to a corresponding limit or reduction under the law of a country outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(3) the cap applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the damages would have been awarded in an action brought in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage against the person from whom the contribution is sought` AND (`they were or would have been subject to a limit imposed by or under any written law or by an agreement made before the damage occurred` OR `they were or would have been subject to a reduction by virtue of section 3 of the Contributory Negligence and Personal Injuries Act 1953` OR `they were or would have been subject to a corresponding limit or reduction under the law of a country outside Singapore`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the amount of the damages which have or might have been awarded ... was or would have been subject to — (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..., the person from whom the contribution is sought shall not ... be required to pay ... a greater amount" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b))

-- src:1185 | (3) Where the amount of the damages which have or might have
-- src:1186 | been awarded in respect of the damage in question in any action
-- src:1187 | brought in Singapore by or on behalf of the person who suffered it
-- src:1188 | against the person from whom the contribution is sought was or
-- src:1189 | would have been subject to —
-- src:1191 | (a) any limit imposed by or under any written law or by any
-- src:1192 | agreement made before the damage occurred;
-- src:1197 | (b) any reduction by virtue of section 3 of the Contributory
-- src:1198 | Negligence and Personal Injuries Act 1953; or
-- src:1200 | (c) any corresponding limit or reduction under the law of a
-- src:1201 | country outside Singapore,
-- src:1203 | the person from whom the contribution is sought shall not, by virtue
-- src:1204 | of any contribution awarded under section 15, be required to pay in
-- src:1205 | respect of the damage a greater amount than the amount of those
-- src:1206 | damages as so limited or reduced.
@ref s 16(3) the bar (src:1185-1206)
GIVEN `the cap applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount sought` IS A NUMBER
      `the damages as so limited or reduced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(3) the person is required to pay a greater amount than the damages as so limited or reduced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cap applies` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the amount of the damages ... was or would have been subject to"
        IF `the amount sought` GREATER THAN `the damages as so limited or reduced` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person from whom the contribution is sought shall not, by virtue of any contribution awarded under section 15, be required to pay in respect of the damage a greater amount than the amount of those damages as so limited or reduced"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an amount within the limit is not addressed by the subsection

§ `Sections 17 and 18 -- proceedings against persons jointly liable; successive actions`

-- src:1211 | 17. Judgment recovered against any person liable in respect of any
-- src:1212 | debt or damage shall not be a bar to an action, or to the continuance of
-- src:1213 | an action, against any other person who is (apart from any such bar)
-- src:1214 | jointly liable with him in respect of the same debt or damage.
@ref s 17 (src:1211-1214)
GIVEN `the other person is jointly liable with him in respect of the same debt or damage apart from any such bar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 the judgment recovered against the person is a bar to an action or to the continuance of an action against the other person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the other person is jointly liable with him in respect of the same debt or damage apart from any such bar` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Judgment recovered against any person liable in respect of any debt or damage shall not be a bar to an action, or to the continuance of an action, against any other person who is (apart from any such bar) jointly liable with him in respect of the same debt or damage"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other person who is (apart from any such bar) jointly liable with him"

-- src:1219 | 18. If more than one action is brought in respect of any damage by
-- src:1220 | or on behalf of the person by whom it was suffered against persons
-- src:1221 | liable in respect of the damage (whether jointly or otherwise) the
-- src:1222 | claimant shall not be entitled to costs in any of those actions, other
-- src:1223 | than that in which judgment is first given, unless the court is of the
-- src:1224 | opinion that there was reasonable ground for bringing the action.
@ref s 18 (src:1219-1224)
GIVEN `more than one action is brought in respect of the damage by or on behalf of the person by whom it was suffered against persons liable in respect of the damage whether jointly or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `judgment is first given in this action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for bringing the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18 the claimant is entitled to costs in the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `more than one action is brought in respect of the damage by or on behalf of the person by whom it was suffered against persons liable in respect of the damage whether jointly or otherwise` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If more than one action is brought in respect of any damage"
        IF `judgment is first given in this action` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than that in which judgment is first given" -- an excepted action is outside the bar and so grants nothing (fork QA, QE)
        IF `the court is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for bringing the action` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the court is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for bringing the action" -- a lifted bar grants nothing (fork QA); see the companion s 18 the claimant is barred from costs in the action
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the claimant shall not be entitled to costs in any of those actions"

-- src:1219 | 18. If more than one action is brought in respect of any damage by
-- src:1220 | or on behalf of the person by whom it was suffered against persons
-- src:1221 | liable in respect of the damage (whether jointly or otherwise) the
-- src:1222 | claimant shall not be entitled to costs in any of those actions, other
-- src:1223 | than that in which judgment is first given, unless the court is of the
-- src:1224 | opinion that there was reasonable ground for bringing the action.
@ref s 18 the bar as a yes/no question (src:1219-1224)
GIVEN `more than one action is brought in respect of the damage by or on behalf of the person by whom it was suffered against persons liable in respect of the damage whether jointly or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `judgment is first given in this action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for bringing the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18 the claimant is barred from costs in the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `more than one action is brought in respect of the damage by or on behalf of the person by whom it was suffered against persons liable in respect of the damage whether jointly or otherwise` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If more than one action is brought in respect of any damage"
        IF `judgment is first given in this action` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be entitled to costs in any of those actions, other than that in which judgment is first given" -- the bar is stated not to reach the action in which judgment is first given, just as the "unless" below lifts it (fork QE: the other reading is NOTHING, a scope carve-out)
        IF `the court is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for bringing the action` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for bringing the action" -- the bar does not apply
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 19 -- interpretation and application of sections 15 to 18`

-- src:1230 | 19.—(1) A person is liable in respect of any damage for the
-- src:1231 | purposes of sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 if the person who suffered it (or
-- src:1232 | anyone representing his estate or dependants) is entitled to recover
-- src:1233 | compensation from him in respect of that damage (whatever the legal
-- src:1234 | basis of this liability), whether tort, breach of contract, breach of trust
-- src:1235 | or otherwise).
@ref s 19(1) (src:1230-1235)
GIVEN `the person who suffered the damage or anyone representing his estate or dependants is entitled to recover compensation from the person in respect of that damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(1) the person is liable in respect of the damage for the purposes of sections 15 to 18` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person who suffered the damage or anyone representing his estate or dependants is entitled to recover compensation from the person in respect of that damage` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is liable in respect of any damage for the purposes of sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 if the person who suffered it (or anyone representing his estate or dependants) is entitled to recover compensation from him in respect of that damage" -- MARGINAL (a): a definition by "if" read as the whole of it

-- src:1233 | compensation from him in respect of that damage (whatever the legal
-- src:1234 | basis of this liability), whether tort, breach of contract, breach of trust
-- src:1235 | or otherwise).
@ref s 19(1) the legal basis (src:1233-1235)
GIVEN `the person who suffered the damage or anyone representing his estate or dependants is entitled to recover compensation from the person in respect of that damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(1) the legal basis of the liability matters` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person who suffered the damage or anyone representing his estate or dependants is entitled to recover compensation from the person in respect of that damage` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(whatever the legal basis of this liability), whether tort, breach of contract, breach of trust or otherwise"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whatever the legal basis"

-- src:1237 | (2) References in sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 to an action brought by
-- src:1238 | or on behalf of the person who suffered any damage include
-- src:1239 | references to an action brought for the benefit of his estate or
-- src:1240 | dependants.
@ref s 19(2) (src:1237-1240)
GIVEN `the action is brought by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is brought for the benefit of his estate or dependants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(2) the action is an action brought by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the action is brought by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage` OR `the action is brought for the benefit of his estate or dependants` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include references to an action brought for the benefit of his estate or dependants"

-- src:1245 | (3) For the purposes of sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 —
-- src:1247 | (a) “dependants” has the same meaning as in section 20; and
@ref s 19(3)(a) (src:1245-1247)
GIVEN `the relationship to the deceased` IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(3)(a) the person is a dependant for the purposes of sections 15 to 18` MEANS
    `s 20(8) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `the relationship to the deceased`

-- src:1245 | (3) For the purposes of sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 —
-- src:1249 | (b) except in section 15(5), “action” means an action brought
-- src:1250 | in Singapore.
@ref s 19(3)(b) (src:1245-1250)
GIVEN `the reference is in section 15(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is brought in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(3)(b) the action is an action within the meaning of sections 15 to 18` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the reference is in section 15(5)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in section 15(5)"
        IF `the action is brought in Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“action” means an action brought in Singapore"

-- src:1252 | (4) Nothing in sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 shall affect any case where
-- src:1253 | the debt in question became due or, as the case may be, the damage in
-- src:1254 | question occurred before 1 January 1999.
@ref s 19(4) (src:1252-1254)
GIVEN `the date on which the debt became due or the damage occurred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(4) sections 15 to 18 affect the case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date on which the debt became due or the damage occurred` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 1999)) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 shall affect any case where the debt in question became due or, as the case may be, the damage in question occurred before 1 January 1999"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says what the sections do not affect and says nothing of a later case

-- src:1256 | (5) A person shall not be entitled to recover contribution or be liable
-- src:1257 | to make contribution in accordance with section 15 by reference to
-- src:1258 | any liability based on breach of any obligation assumed by him before
-- src:1259 | 1 January 1999.
@ref s 19(5) (src:1256-1259)
GIVEN `the date on which the obligation was assumed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(5) the person is entitled to recover or liable to make contribution by reference to the liability` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date on which the obligation was assumed` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 1999)) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person shall not be entitled to recover contribution or be liable to make contribution in accordance with section 15 by reference to any liability based on breach of any obligation assumed by him before 1 January 1999"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any liability based on breach of any obligation assumed by him before 1 January 1999"

-- src:1261 | (6) The right to recover contribution in accordance with section 15
-- src:1262 | supersedes any right, other than an express contractual right, to
-- src:1263 | recover contribution (as distinct from indemnity) otherwise than
-- src:1264 | under sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 in corresponding circumstances; but
@ref s 19(6) (src:1261-1264)
GIVEN `the other right is a right to recover contribution as distinct from indemnity otherwise than under sections 15 to 18 in corresponding circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other right is an express contractual right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(6) the right to recover contribution in accordance with section 15 supersedes the other right` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the other right is a right to recover contribution as distinct from indemnity otherwise than under sections 15 to 18 in corresponding circumstances` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any right ... to recover contribution (as distinct from indemnity) otherwise than under sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 in corresponding circumstances"
        IF `the other right is an express contractual right` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "supersedes any right, other than an express contractual right" -- fork QE: the carve-out is in the text's own words ("other than"), so an express contractual right gets JUST FALSE (the other reading is NOTHING, as for a scope limit)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1264 | under sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 in corresponding circumstances; but
-- src:1265 | nothing in sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 shall affect —
-- src:1267 | (a) any express or implied contractual or other right to
-- src:1268 | indemnity; or
@ref s 19(6)(a) (src:1264-1268)
GIVEN `the right is an express or implied contractual or other right to indemnity which would be enforceable apart from sections 15 to 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(6)(a) sections 15 to 18 affect the right to indemnity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the right is an express or implied contractual or other right to indemnity which would be enforceable apart from sections 15 to 18` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 shall affect — (a) any express or implied contractual or other right to indemnity"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which would be enforceable apart from sections 15, 16, 17 and 18"

-- src:1264 | under sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 in corresponding circumstances; but
-- src:1265 | nothing in sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 shall affect —
-- src:1270 | (b) any express contractual provision regulating or excluding
-- src:1271 | contribution,
-- src:1273 | which would be enforceable apart from sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 (or
@ref s 19(6)(b) (src:1264-1273)
GIVEN `the provision is an express contractual provision regulating or excluding contribution which would be enforceable apart from sections 15 to 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(6)(b) sections 15 to 18 affect the contractual provision regulating or excluding contribution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision is an express contractual provision regulating or excluding contribution which would be enforceable apart from sections 15 to 18` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 shall affect — ... (b) any express contractual provision regulating or excluding contribution"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which would be enforceable apart from sections 15, 16, 17 and 18"

-- src:1264 | under sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 in corresponding circumstances; but
-- src:1265 | nothing in sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 shall affect —
-- src:1273 | which would be enforceable apart from sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 (or
-- src:1274 | render enforceable any agreement for indemnity or contribution
-- src:1275 | which would not be enforceable apart from sections 15, 16, 17 and
-- src:1276 | 18).
@ref s 19(6) the agreement made enforceable (src:1264-1276)
GIVEN `the agreement for indemnity or contribution would not be enforceable apart from sections 15 to 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(6) sections 15 to 18 render enforceable the agreement for indemnity or contribution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the agreement for indemnity or contribution would not be enforceable apart from sections 15 to 18` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in sections 15, 16, 17 and 18 shall ... render enforceable any agreement for indemnity or contribution which would not be enforceable apart from sections 15, 16, 17 and 18"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any agreement for indemnity or contribution which would not be enforceable apart from sections 15, 16, 17 and 18"

§§ `Sections 15 to 19 -- tests`

-- s 15
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the person may recover contribution from the other person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "may recover contribution from any other person liable in respect of the same damage"
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the person may recover contribution from the other person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the other person is not liable for the same damage
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the person may recover contribution from the other person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the person is not liable
#ASSERT `s 15(2) the person is entitled to recover contribution although he has ceased to be liable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- ceased to be liable but liable immediately before the payment
#ASSERT `s 15(2) the person is entitled to recover contribution although he has ceased to be liable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "provided that he was so liable immediately before"
#ASSERT `s 15(2) the person is entitled to recover contribution although he has ceased to be liable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- has not ceased to be liable
#ASSERT `s 15(3) the person is liable to make contribution although he has ceased to be liable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be liable to make contribution ... notwithstanding"
#ASSERT `s 15(3) the person is liable to make contribution although he has ceased to be liable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "unless he ceased to be liable by virtue of the expiry of a period of limitation"
#ASSERT `s 15(3) the person is liable to make contribution although he has ceased to be liable` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- has not ceased to be liable
#ASSERT `s 15(4) the person is entitled to recover contribution in accordance with section 15 whether or not he was liable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a bona fide settlement
#ASSERT `s 15(4) the person is entitled to recover contribution in accordance with section 15 whether or not he was liable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "provided, however, that he would have been liable"
#ASSERT `s 15(4) the person is entitled to recover contribution in accordance with section 15 whether or not he was liable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- no settlement
#ASSERT `s 15(5) the judgment is conclusive in the proceedings for contribution in favour of the person from whom contribution is sought` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be conclusive"
#ASSERT `s 15(5) the judgment is conclusive in the proceedings for contribution in favour of the person from whom contribution is sought` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "provided that the judgment in his favour rested on a determination of the merits"
#ASSERT `s 15(5) the judgment is conclusive in the proceedings for contribution in favour of the person from whom contribution is sought` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a judgment of that kind
#ASSERT `s 15(6) the liability is a liability in respect of damage for the purposes of section 15` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- established or could be established in Singapore
#ASSERT `s 15(6) the liability is a liability in respect of damage for the purposes of section 15` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "references to any such liability which has been or could be established"
#ASSERT `s 15(6) it matters that an issue was or would be determined by reference to the law of a country outside Singapore` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "it is immaterial"
#ASSERT `s 15(6) it matters that an issue was or would be determined by reference to the law of a country outside Singapore` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no foreign law in issue
-- s 16
#ASSERT `s 16(1) the amount of the contribution is the amount the court finds just and equitable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "just and equitable having regard to the extent of that person's responsibility"
#ASSERT `s 16(1) the amount of the contribution is the amount the court finds just and equitable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a bare "shall be" (QB)
#ASSERT `s 16(1) the amount of the contribution is the amount the court finds just and equitable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not proceedings for contribution
#ASSERT `s 16(2) the court has power to exempt the person from liability to make contribution or to direct a complete indemnity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall have power"
#ASSERT `s 16(2) the court has power to exempt the person from liability to make contribution or to direct a complete indemnity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not such proceedings
#ASSERT `s 16(3) the cap applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a statutory limit
#ASSERT `s 16(3) the cap applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a reduction under the Contributory Negligence and Personal Injuries Act 1953
#ASSERT `s 16(3) the cap applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a corresponding foreign limit
#ASSERT `s 16(3) the cap applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no limit or reduction: "Where"
#ASSERT `s 16(3) the cap applies` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not an action brought in Singapore
#ASSERT `s 16(3) the most the person is required to pay in respect of the damage by virtue of the contribution` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 8000 5000 EQUALS JUST 5000 -- the contribution is cut back to the limited damages
#ASSERT `s 16(3) the most the person is required to pay in respect of the damage by virtue of the contribution` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 3000 5000 EQUALS JUST 3000 -- a contribution within the limit is unchanged
#ASSERT `s 16(3) the most the person is required to pay in respect of the damage by virtue of the contribution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 8000 5000 EQUALS NOTHING -- no limit or reduction: the cap does not apply
#ASSERT `s 16(3) the person is required to pay a greater amount than the damages as so limited or reduced` TRUE 8000 5000 EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not ... be required to pay ... a greater amount"
#ASSERT `s 16(3) the person is required to pay a greater amount than the damages as so limited or reduced` TRUE 5000 5000 EQUALS NOTHING -- an amount within the limit: silent
#ASSERT `s 16(3) the person is required to pay a greater amount than the damages as so limited or reduced` FALSE 8000 5000 EQUALS NOTHING -- the cap does not apply
-- s 17, 18
#ASSERT `s 17 the judgment recovered against the person is a bar to an action or to the continuance of an action against the other person` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not be a bar"
#ASSERT `s 17 the judgment recovered against the person is a bar to an action or to the continuance of an action against the other person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a jointly liable person
#ASSERT `s 18 the claimant is entitled to costs in the action` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not be entitled to costs in any of those actions"
#ASSERT `s 18 the claimant is entitled to costs in the action` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the action in which judgment is first given
#ASSERT `s 18 the claimant is entitled to costs in the action` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- reasonable ground: "unless" met, a lifted bar grants nothing (QA)
#ASSERT `s 18 the claimant is entitled to costs in the action` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- only one action
#ASSERT `s 18 the claimant is barred from costs in the action` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- barred
#ASSERT `s 18 the claimant is barred from costs in the action` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- reasonable ground: the bar does not apply
#ASSERT `s 18 the claimant is barred from costs in the action` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the action in which judgment is first given: the bar is stated not to reach it, as the "unless" lifts it (fork QE)
#ASSERT `s 18 the claimant is barred from costs in the action` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- only one action
-- s 19
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the person is liable in respect of the damage for the purposes of sections 15 to 18` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- entitled to recover compensation
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the person is liable in respect of the damage for the purposes of sections 15 to 18` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not entitled: "if"
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the legal basis of the liability matters` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "whatever the legal basis"
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the legal basis of the liability matters` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no entitlement to compensation
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the action is an action brought by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- by or on behalf of that person
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the action is an action brought by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- for the benefit of his estate or dependants
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the action is an action brought by or on behalf of the person who suffered the damage` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "include" does not close the list
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(a) the person is a dependant for the purposes of sections 15 to 18` `The wife or husband of the deceased` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the same meaning as in section 20
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(a) the person is a dependant for the purposes of sections 15 to 18` `Another relationship` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the same meaning as in section 20
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(b) the action is an action within the meaning of sections 15 to 18` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an action brought in Singapore
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(b) the action is an action within the meaning of sections 15 to 18` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "means an action brought in Singapore"
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(b) the action is an action within the meaning of sections 15 to 18` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "except in section 15(5)"
#ASSERT `s 19(4) sections 15 to 18 affect the case` (Date 31 12 1998) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- before 1 January 1999
#ASSERT `s 19(4) sections 15 to 18 affect the case` (Date 1 1 1999) EQUALS NOTHING -- on 1 January 1999: the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is entitled to recover or liable to make contribution by reference to the liability` (Date 31 12 1998) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- an obligation assumed before 1 January 1999
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is entitled to recover or liable to make contribution by reference to the liability` (Date 1 1 1999) EQUALS NOTHING -- on 1 January 1999: the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 19(6) the right to recover contribution in accordance with section 15 supersedes the other right` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- supersedes
#ASSERT `s 19(6) the right to recover contribution in accordance with section 15 supersedes the other right` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "other than an express contractual right"
#ASSERT `s 19(6) the right to recover contribution in accordance with section 15 supersedes the other right` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a right to contribution
#ASSERT `s 19(6)(a) sections 15 to 18 affect the right to indemnity` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "nothing ... shall affect"
#ASSERT `s 19(6)(a) sections 15 to 18 affect the right to indemnity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a right not enforceable apart from the sections
#ASSERT `s 19(6)(b) sections 15 to 18 affect the contractual provision regulating or excluding contribution` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "nothing ... shall affect"
#ASSERT `s 19(6)(b) sections 15 to 18 affect the contractual provision regulating or excluding contribution` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another provision
#ASSERT `s 19(6) sections 15 to 18 render enforceable the agreement for indemnity or contribution` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "[nothing shall] render enforceable any agreement ... which would not be enforceable apart from"
#ASSERT `s 19(6) sections 15 to 18 render enforceable the agreement for indemnity or contribution` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an agreement enforceable anyway
